---
title: "cancel (Compound V2: Governor Bravo)"
---
stateDiagram-v2
    direction TB
    [*] --> q_state_check: proposalState = state(proposalId)
    q_state_check --> q_executed: proposalState == Executed
    q_executed --> [*]: revert "cannot cancel executed proposal"
    q_state_check --> q_auth_check: proposalState != Executed
    q_auth_check --> q_is_proposer: msg.sender == proposal.proposer
    q_is_proposer --> q_cancel_actions: authorized (proposer can always cancel own proposal)
    q_auth_check --> q_votes_check: msg.sender != proposal.proposer
    q_votes_check --> q_has_votes: proposer votes > proposalThreshold
    q_has_votes --> [*]: revert "proposer above threshold"
    q_votes_check --> q_cancel_actions: proposer votes <= proposalThreshold
    q_cancel_actions --> q_iter: for each action in proposal
    q_iter --> q_cancel_tx: timelock.cancelTransaction(target, value, signature, data, eta)
    q_cancel_tx --> q_iter: next action
    q_iter --> q_finalize: all actions canceled
    q_finalize --> [*]: proposal.canceled = true; emit ProposalCanceled(proposalId)

    note right of q_auth_check
        INV-001: Proposer can always cancel their own proposal
        INV-002: Anyone can cancel if proposer's votes drop below threshold
        INV-003: Cannot cancel already executed proposals
    end note

    note right of q_cancel_actions
        INV-004: Cancellation removes queued transactions from timelock
        INV-005: Proposal state transitions to Canceled
    end note
